Security Observation
The EC2 security group currently allows SSH access on port 22 from 0.0.0.0/0. This means SSH connection attempts can originate from any IPv4 address, although authentication is still required.
For a production environment, SSH access should normally be restricted to trusted sources where practical.
The EBS root volume was also observed to be unencrypted during this practical. This is an important security observation because encryption helps protect stored data.

